  "output": {
    "answer": "After that failure I added a real-device check as a standing step, not a one-off reaction: before calling any UI work DONE, someone re-walks the built screens on one real device, in the real flow, checking for what a simulated viewport hides — browser chrome eating space, a modal reopening every task, options only reachable after rotating the phone. That's now the last gate before done, every time, not just after a failure. What the record doesn't say is whether it's always a human doing that walk versus an agent standing in — the excerpts only establish that the real-device pass itself is mandatory before DONE.",
